From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Ericson <John.Ericson@Obsidian.Systems>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 11:49:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] cmd/make: find arch(1) and mach(1) on `$PATH`

`init_arch_macros()` and `init_mach_macros()` popen(3C) `/bin/mach` and
`/bin/arch` by absolute path to fill in `$(HOST_ARCH)` and `$(HOST_MACH)`.
Both are ordinary commands; naming them without a directory lets a build
that is not rooted at `/` -- a foreign build host, or a build against a
staged proto area -- supply its own.

Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5 (claude-opus-5)
---
 usr/src/cmd/make/lib/mksh/macro.cc | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/usr/src/cmd/make/lib/mksh/macro.cc b/usr/src/cmd/make/lib/mksh/macro.cc
index 24e3a453ba..f385b6ad95 100644
--- a/usr/src/cmd/make/lib/mksh/macro.cc
+++ b/usr/src/cmd/make/lib/mksh/macro.cc
@@ -904,7 +904,7 @@ init_arch_macros(void)
 	FILE		*pipe;
 	Name		value;
 	int		set_host, set_target;
-	const char	*mach_command = "/bin/mach";
+	const char	*mach_command = "mach";
 
 	set_host = (get_prop(host_arch->prop, macro_prop) == NULL);
 	set_target = (get_prop(target_arch->prop, macro_prop) == NULL);
@@ -959,7 +959,7 @@ init_mach_macros(void)
 	FILE		*pipe;
 	Name		value;
 	int		set_host, set_target;
-	const char	*arch_command = "/bin/arch";
+	const char	*arch_command = "arch";
 
 	set_host = (get_prop(host_mach->prop, macro_prop) == NULL);
 	set_target = (get_prop(target_mach->prop, macro_prop) == NULL);
